    plainEnglish: 'The mandatory cash payouts an employer must legally pay to an employee when their employment is terminated.',
    legalDefinition: 'The tripartite statutory post-termination compensation package mandated under Indonesian employment law payable to permanent employees upon dismissal: (1) Uang Pesangon (Severance Pay), (2) Uang Penghargaan Masa Kerja / UPMK (Long Service Pay), and (3) Uang Penggantian Hak / UPH (Compensation for Accrued Rights such as unused annual leave).',
    indonesianLegalConcept: 'Formula perhitungan kompensasi pemutusan hubungan kerja (PHK) yang diatur secara rinci dalam Pasal 156 UU Ketenagakerjaan jo. PP No. 35/2021, dengan pengali yang bervariasi tergantung alasan PHK (efisiensi, pailit, merger, pensiun, atau pelanggaran disiplin).',
    legalFunction: 'Provides an essential economic safety net for laid-off workers and establishes strict financial discipline on corporate redundancy decisions.',
    exampleSentenceEn: 'Following the corporate restructuring, the dismissed staff received their full statutory entitlements comprising severance pay, service pay, and accrued leave compensation.',
    exampleSentenceId: 'Menyusul restrukturisasi korporasi, staf yang terkena PHK menerima hak statutori penuh mereka yang terdiri dari uang pesangon, uang penghargaan masa kerja, dan uang penggantian hak.',
    authenticClauseExcerpt: 'Upon termination of employment, the Company shall pay to the Employee severance pay (Uang Pesangon), long service pay (UPMK), and compensation of rights (UPH) strictly in accordance with PP No. 35 of 2021.',
    authenticClauseSource: 'Company Regulation (Peraturan Perusahaan) & Mutual Termination Agreement',
    commonMistakesOrNuances: 'Resigning voluntarily (mengundurkan diri atas kemauan sendiri) does NOT entitle a worker to severance pay (Uang Pesangon), only to UPH and Uang Pisah if agreed in the company regulation.',
    commonCollocations: ['statutory severance calculation', 'UPMK and UPH entitlements', 'mutual separation agreement (PB PHK)', 'PP 35/2021 severance formula'],
